                                                "sense_id": "6066f546-0728-3279-a371-aea872bec19c",
                                                "text": "Port your helm!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a7932ae-5ce6-3a05-ab43-a04fcaf23d16",
                                        "entry_id": "20f1e799-7599-33b7-aa64-f5c4dfe58d9e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dock at a port."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc05e986-9a06-458d-9442-868de23a5c1a",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7932ae-5ce6-3a05-ab43-a04fcaf23d16",
                                                "text": "The tall ships will port in Pugwash during its annual Harbourfest Celebrations[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6729e51b-bdcd-48f5-a098-4e49123a41f9",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7932ae-5ce6-3a05-ab43-a04fcaf23d16",
                                                "text": "We have to wait until the ship ports, buddy, and then we can get you the help you need."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "147f7820-9cf0-4a42-99ee-379e5a2ae161",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7932ae-5ce6-3a05-ab43-a04fcaf23d16",
                                                "text": "Our cruise ship ported at Mykonos, a small island off the coast of Greece, for an overnight stay."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "port",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be513f8e-ba65-3688-9359-0a24526f67d2",
                                        "entry_id": "92fe3e4e-8a65-3283-bfd4-49f67a853e1d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An entryway or gate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58f1862d-cc46-46de-a7a9-20a913be759a",
                                                "sense_id": "be513f8e-ba65-3688-9359-0a24526f67d2",
                                                "text": "And whan he cam to the porte of the pavelon, Sir Palomydes seyde an hyghe, ‘Where art thou, Sir Trystram de Lyones?’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74290ee4-6c04-4235-af88-7e242c4e2b3a",
                                                "sense_id": "be513f8e-ba65-3688-9359-0a24526f67d2",
                                                "text": "Long were it to describe the goodly frame, / And stately port of Castle Joyeous […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3b65dcf-8106-4b04-8cc1-e4d2291473a7",
                                                "sense_id": "be513f8e-ba65-3688-9359-0a24526f67d2",
                                                "text": "Him I accuse / The city ports by this hath enter'd"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0aa8f622-80cf-4e17-a869-0d7cf1af0659",
                                                "sense_id": "be513f8e-ba65-3688-9359-0a24526f67d2",
                                                "text": "And from their ivory port the Cherubim, / Forth issuing at the accustomed hour"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0903a71a-a95a-3033-ad17-16afd36d80bc",
                                        "entry_id": "92fe3e4e-8a65-3283-bfd4-49f67a853e1d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An opening or doorway in the side of a ship, especially for boarding or loading; an embrasure through which a cannon may be discharged; a porthole."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd83dfd4-8b2a-4c1c-8c85-b9aad1c16e15",
                                                "sense_id": "0903a71a-a95a-3033-ad17-16afd36d80bc",
                                                "text": "[…] her ports being within sixteen inches of the water […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6152c3ad-5e7b-39b6-ac1c-96134258cabd",
